= Joint Campaigning

Campaigning alongside other parties is an opportunity to reach out to their base – and for them to reach out to ours. Who should we coordinate our campaign efforts with?

- @new_middle: The DDP, with their base in the "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers.
- @old_middle: The DVP, with their base in the "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @unemployed: The USPD, with their base in the unemployed.
- @catholics: The Center Party, with their powerful Catholic base.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1 and ddp_relation >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: We either do not have enough resources or not enough relations with the DDP.
on-arrival: new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); workers_dvp += 2; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1;

Campaigning alongside the DDP, we have increased our campaigning among the new middle class. Our campaign partners lend us credibility.

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1 and dvp_relation >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: We either do not have enough resources or not enough relations with the DVP.
on-arrival: old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); workers_dvp += 2; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1

Campaigning alongside the DVP, we have increased our campaigning among the old middle class. Our campaign partners lend us credibility.

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1 and USPD_relation >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: We either do not have enough resources or not enough relations with the USPD.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 5*(1-dissent); workers_uspd += 2; resources -= 1;

Campaigning alongside the USPD, we have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. Our campaign partners lend us credibility.

